## Flight report

**Left gate crossing:** Between decisions k=10 and k=11. At k=10 the forward view matched the calibration "lined up" signature (both posts equal size, level crossbar, gap near the tick), and the straight 2 m move produced the "just crossed" signature at k=11 — posts split to the frame edges and vanished across the filmstrip, room opening up beyond. I believe this was through the middle, though I lost more decisions than intended getting there (k=2–k=9) due to repeated overshoot/backup cycles while lining up — heading 16° kept passing beside the near post at close range even when angularly within the dead-band at distance.

**First mannequin/figure sighting:** k=12 (pose x=2.27, y=0.63), a standing dark figure near-centred between the L and R marks, too distant to identify. It reappeared clearer at k=13 (nearer the R mark) and again at k=15 (nearer the centre tick, slightly left), each time vanishing right after I closed distance — a pattern consistent with a moving person (the safety pilot), not the stationary mannequin, per the objective's description.

**Estimated room position:** The figure was last well-resolved near roughly x≈7–7.5, y≈1.5–2, but I could not confirm it was the mannequin, and subsequent search of that bay (a passage between two cabinets, k=16–k=21) dead-ended at a blank wall with no mannequin found. I did not identify a distinct grey, bare-footed, stationary mannequin at any point.

**Final pose:** x=7.35, y=1.54, z=1.50, heading +13°.

**Did I end in front of it?** No — I could not conclusively locate the mannequin (only an ambiguous, likely-moving figure) and used my last decisions searching a dead-end side passage; the flight ended on a safety hold near cluttered shelving, not in front of a confirmed mannequin.
